# Cheat Sheet Template (Canonical)

**Audience:** Engineers who **already know** the topic. Goal = **brush up** — syntax, tables, snippets. Not tutorials.

## Separate From

| Format | Sections | Examples |
|---|---|---|
| **Cheat sheet** | This rule | Java, Python, Go, Spring Boot, K8s CLI |
| **Playbook** | Why, flows, trade-offs, code-tabs | Microservices, System Design |
| **Interview** | Long-form Q&A | Interview Prep |

Do **not** use playbook sections (Why It Exists, Request Flow essays) on cheat sheets.

## Hugo Front Matter

```yaml
cheatSheet: true
ShowToc: true
categories: ["<Section Title>"]
tags: ["cheatsheet", "handbook", ...]
```

## Required Sections (`##` headings)

1. **At a Glance** — 3–5 bullets max
2. **Reference Tables** — primary content; club related basics on one page
3. **Snippets** — minimal copy-paste; constructor injection for Java; one language per page
4. **Internals & Gotchas** — short bullets
5. **Production Notes** — ops tips (optional if truly N/A)
6. **Interview Probes** — `{{< interview-answer >}}` 0–2 per page; full FAQ → Interview module only
7. **See Also** — prev/next + index

Separate with `---`. Use `note` / `tip` / `warning` sparingly.

## Clubbing Rules

| Do club on one page | Do not split |
|---|---|
| Primitives + syntax + variables | Per-annotation pages for Spring |
| All HTTP mapping annotations | "Creating a project" tutorials |
| Repository hierarchy + paging | Beginner install guides |

## Omit

- "How to create a project" walkthroughs (one-row bootstrap table is enough)
- Long Mermaid lifecycle diagrams (tiny diagrams in tables OK)
- `{{< code-tabs >}}` multi-language tabs (playbook only)
- Core Java / DSA / design patterns (other sections)

## Section-Specific Rules

- Java: `java-cheatsheet-posts.mdc`
- Spring Boot: `spring-boot-handbook-posts.mdc`
- K8s/Docker: `engineering-handbook-cheatsheets.mdc`

## Regenerate

Each section has `scripts/build_<section>_*.py` — hand edits overwritten on regen unless you update the build script.
